$DIR/main.p:18:9: cannot return h.mk(&in), which points into in, a local variable of g
    h.mk(&in) points into in. in is a local variable of g (declared at
    main.p:16). Its memory is reclaimed when g returns, so h.mk(&in) would point
    at memory that no longer holds in.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Return values instead of views of in, or allocate in and return its owner,
    an owned[Inner]:
        in := new(Inner)
        ...
        return in
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3001" for a longer explanation)
